{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For the vineyards.</b> Like וּמֵשְׁדֵמֹת עֲמֹרָה (Deuteronomy 32:32), like vines." "<b>Are wilted.</b> Each one." "<b>The lords of the nations.</b> Like אֲדֹנֵי יוֹסֵף (Genesis 39:20), כֶּסֶף יָשִׁיב לְבַעֲלָיו (Exodus —); and they are the kings of Assyria." "<b>Struck its shoots.</b> Struck, like וְהָלְמָה סִיסְרָא (Judges 5:26)." "<b>Reached to Jazer.</b> So wide they were." "<b>Wandered the desert.</b> For they spread until a place where there is no settlement." "<b>Its branches.</b> Its trees, like שְׁלָחַיִךְ פַּרְדֵּס רִמּוֹנִים (Song of Songs 4:13)." "<b>Were cast out.</b> Like וְהִנָּם נְטוּשִׁים (1 Samuel 30:15), spread out."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {2 "The citation שמות כ\"ד ל\"ד does not correspond to the quoted phrase in Exodus; the reference appears erroneous in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:05.951951596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}